<svelte:head><title>Build and contribute — Voynich@home</title></svelte:head>
<div class="page narrow prose"><p class="eyebrow">Open code, explicit contracts</p><h1>Make it reproducible.</h1><p class="lede">The Rust kernel runs the science. The browser uses WebAssembly from the same source. SvelteKit connects participants to bounded, checked work.</p><h2>Build locally</h2><p>Use the pinned Rust toolchain and Node 22 or newer. Setup, data provenance, and development examples live with the source.</p><pre>git clone https://github.com/javidmardanov/VoynichAtHome.git
cd VoynichAtHome
git checkout codex/public-release
cd kernel
cargo test --workspace
cargo build --release</pre><p>Run a declared search using its complete input, including the quantized language model:</p><pre>vah-search run --job job.json --out result.json</pre><p>This command does not receive the hidden original message or encoding key. Compare its output against the answer in the separate evaluation harness.</p><h2>Useful contributions</h2><ul><li>Review the source-work splits and normalization rules for Latin and Italian.</li><li>Improve bounded search methods and compare them under the same budgets.</li><li>Reproduce a published record on a different browser or native platform.</li><li>Test keyboard access, mobile layouts, offline recovery, and operating procedures.</li></ul><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://github.com/javidmardanov/VoynichAtHome">Browse the source ↗</a><a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/javidmardanov/VoynichAtHome/issues">Find or report a task ↗</a></div><h2>Code and data rights</h2><p>Original project code uses the MIT license. Imported code, transcriptions, comparison texts, images, and fonts keep their own terms. The repository records their sources and hashes separately. No manuscript images or third-party fonts are bundled in this interface.</p><a href="https://github.com/javidmardanov/VoynichAtHome/blob/codex/public-release/docs/LICENSING.md">Read the rights and provenance register ↗</a><h2>Release downloads</h2><p>There is no declared production release yet. Build from a recorded commit for development; release binaries, signatures, and provenance will be published together after the release checks pass.</p></div>
